    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207-a3">

                <pb facs="1257" n="1099" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1099"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Thompson to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-10-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                    1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your excellency’s courteous note, dated the 10th instant,
                    transmitting copy of a communication from the department of war and marine
                    disproving the rumors that Mexican war vessels had been ordered to capture
                    foreign fishing craft found within the territorial waters of this Republic,
                    regardless of the conditions of the weather, and to thank you for this
                    information.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David E.
                    Thompson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
